---
import SectionPageHeader from
  "../components/SectionPageHeader.astro";

import SiteLayout from
  "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Acknowledgements"
  description="Credits, licensing, privacy information, and disclaimers for Fabrizio's Webhome."
  lang="en"
  contentClass="acknowledgements-main"
>
  <SectionPageHeader
    title="Acknowledgements"
    subtitle="About This Site"
    introduction={`Credits, sources, terms of reuse,
and a few necessary caveats.`}
  />

  <article class="acknowledgements-page">
    <section
      class="acknowledgements-page__section acknowledgements-page__section--wide"
      aria-labelledby="about-this-webhome"
    >
      <h2 id="about-this-webhome">
        About this Webhome
      </h2>

      <p>
        Fabrizio’s Webhome is a personal and evolving
        collection of projects, thoughts, experiments,
        games, and other artifacts by Fabrizio Caragiulo.
        It was conceived as a place in which unfinished
        processes may remain visible alongside completed
        work.
      </p>

      <p>
        The site was designed and developed iteratively
        by Fabrizio Caragiulo with assistance from
        OpenAI Codex. Editorial decisions, published
        materials, and final responsibility for the
        site remain Fabrizio’s.
      </p>

      <p>
        The website is built with
        {" "}
        <a href="https://astro.build/">
          Astro
        </a>,
        TypeScript, HTML, and CSS. Font files are
        self-hosted, partly through
        {" "}
        <a href="https://fontsource.org/">
          Fontsource
        </a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      class="acknowledgements-page__section acknowledgements-page__section--wide"
      aria-labelledby="credits"
    >
      <h2 id="credits">
        Credits
      </h2>

      <h3>Typography</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://velvetyne.fr/fonts/basteleur/">
            Basteleur
          </a>,
          designed by Keussel and distributed by
          Velvetyne Type Foundry.
        </li>

        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/huertatipografica/Alegreya">
            Alegreya
          </a>,
          by the Alegreya Project Authors.
        </li>

        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/productiontype/Spectral">
            Spectral
          </a>,
          by Production Type.
        </li>

        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/arrowtype/recursive">
            Recursive
          </a>,
          by the Recursive Project Authors.
        </li>

        <li>
          Prosto One, by Jovanny Lemonad and
          Pavel Emelyanov.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        These typefaces are distributed under the
        SIL Open Font License 1.1. Their respective
        copyright notices and licence terms remain
        applicable.
      </p>

      <h3>Translations</h3>
      <p>
        Works identified by the <i>Translations</i> tag are translations
        of pre-existing works. Each translation page credits the original
        work and its author or rightsholder, identifies the translator, and
        states the applicable source licence, permission, or public-domain
        status.
      </p>

      <h3>Images and visual materials</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>
          The photographs were taken by
          Fabrizio Caragiulo or E. N. The handwritten
          wordmark is an original work by Fabrizio
          Caragiulo.
        </li>

        <li>
          The animated crow uses the Crow sprite from
          {" "}
          <a href="https://peakpixels.itch.io/commonbirds">
            Common Birds
          </a>
          {" "}
          by Peak Pixels, purchased and used under
          the terms supplied by its author. It is
          excluded from this site’s general content
          licence and is not offered for extraction
          or redistribution.
        </li>

        <li>
        The tile backgrounds are pixel-art
        reinterpretations by Fabrizio Caragiulo,
        based on
        {" "}
        <a href="https://wordpress.org/photos/photo/4636317663/">
            a photograph of Lisbon tile magnets
        </a>
        {" "}
        by Marco Almeida | Webdados, obtained
        from the WordPress Photo Directory and
        released under
        {" "}
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/">
            CC0 1.0
        </a>.
        Attribution is not required, but the
        original photographer is gratefully
        acknowledged.
        </li>

        <li>
          The corner ornament is an SVG adaptation
          by Fabrizio Caragiulo of
          {" "}
          <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vintage_pattern_from_The_Practical_Decorator_and_Ornamentist_by_G.A_%26_M.A._Audsley_from_rawpixel%E2%80%99s_own_original_first_edition_of_the_publication_67.jpg">
            a pattern from <i>The Practical Decorator
            and Ornamentist</i>
          </a>
          {" "}
          by G. A. and M. A. Audsley, from a
          digitisation by Rawpixel. The source image
          and this SVG adaptation are licensed under
          the
          {" "}
          <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">
            Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
            4.0 International licence
          </a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section
      class="acknowledgements-page__section"
      aria-labelledby="disclaimer"
    >
      <h2 id="disclaimer">
        Disclaimer
      </h2>

      <p>
        This is a personal, exploratory, and evolving
        website. Its contents may be incomplete,
        provisional, inaccurate, or revised without
        notice.
      </p>

      <p>
        Nothing published here constitutes financial,
        legal, medical, academic, or other professional
        advice. In particular, portfolio analyses and
        financial experiments are educational works,
        not investment recommendations or guarantees
        of future results.
      </p>

      <p>
        External links are provided for context and
        convenience. They do not imply endorsement,
        and Fabrizio Caragiulo is not responsible for
        the availability, accuracy, or practices of
        third-party websites.
      </p>

      <p>
        To the extent permitted by law, the site and
        its contents are provided “as is”, without
        warranties of any kind.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      class="acknowledgements-page__section"
      aria-labelledby="privacy"
    >
      <h2 id="privacy">
        Privacy
      </h2>

      <p>
        This site does not use analytics, advertising
        trackers, contact forms, or cookies.
      </p>

      <p>
        It uses the browser’s session storage only to
        preserve temporary interface state: the
        continuity of the menu animation and the
        shuffled sequence used by <i>Lega i 4</i>.
        This information remains on the visitor’s
        device and is not transmitted by the site’s
        own code.
      </p>

      <p>
        The hosting provider may process ordinary
        technical request data under its own terms.
        Following an external link or using an email
        link may also involve services governed by
        third-party privacy policies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section
      class="acknowledgements-page__section acknowledgements-page__section--wide"
      aria-labelledby="licensing"
    >
      <h2 id="licensing">
        Copyright and licensing
      </h2>

      <p>
        Unless otherwise stated, original textual and
        visual content by Fabrizio Caragiulo—including
        writings, photographs, crosswords, games, and
        original graphics—is licensed under the
        {" "}
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/">
          Creative Commons
          Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0
          International licence
        </a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        This means that the material may be shared and
        adapted for non-commercial purposes, provided
        that appropriate credit is given, changes are
        indicated, and adaptations are distributed
        under the same or a compatible licence.
      </p>

      <p>
        A suitable attribution is:
        “<i>Title of the work</i>, by Fabrizio
        Caragiulo, from Fabrizio’s Webhome”, followed
        by a link to the original page and to the
        licence.
      </p>

      <p>
        Source code written specifically for this
        website is licensed under the
        {" "}
        <a href="https://opensource.org/license/mit">
          MIT License
        </a>.
        This permission applies to the code, not to
        the site’s editorial content or third-party
        assets.
      </p>

        <p>
        Fonts, software dependencies, purchased
        assets, externally hosted works, and
        materials carrying a separate notice
        remain subject to their respective
        licences. The CV, personal information, 
        the photographs, and the Peak
        Pixels sprite are not included in the 
        general reuse licence.
        Photographs by E. N. are used
        with permission.
        The corner ornament remains licensed
        separately under CC BY-SA 4.0.
        </p>

        <p>
          Translations are excluded from the site’s general CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
          licence unless explicitly stated otherwise on the individual page.
          Copyright and other rights that subsist in the underlying works
          remain with their respective authors or rightsholders. Publication
          on this site does not transfer or waive those rights. Any reuse of
          a translation must comply both with the notice on its individual
          page and with the legal status of the underlying work.
        </p>

      <p>
        © 2026 Fabrizio Caragiulo. Some rights
        reserved.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>